From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:26:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approval): smart approval does not review page_publish

page_publish copies an HTML file into the Hermes page store and the hub shows it as a card to the chat owner. The hub serves a page only through its signed-in, session-checked API route for the owner's own chat, with a sandboxing Content-Security-Policy; there is no public or shareable link (Telegram gets a hub link that needs sign-in). Smart approval still raised an "Unrequested Artifact Publish" card for every call because page_publish was not on the read-only tool list.

page_publish joins READ_ONLY_TOOLS next to send_file, so the provenance review and the hold skip it and its calls stay out of the review transcript. The "Unrequested Artifact Publish" rule now says that delivery to the chat owner's own signed-in chat or hub is not publishing, and names gists, pastes and public file-sharing uploads as covered; hosted pages and public links stay covered. No other tool is added.
